## Payroll generation workflow

1. Select the payroll month.
2. Retrieve eligible drivers.
3. Retrieve the salary structure applicable to each driver for that month.
4. Calculate salary components.
5. Retrieve approved earnings and allowances.
6. Retrieve approved fuel deductions that have not already been posted.
7. Retrieve explicitly authorized advance recoveries.
8. Apply other configured payroll deductions.
9. Calculate gross earnings, total deductions, and net salary.
10. Display payroll validation warnings.
11. Allow review and correction of eligible draft items.
12. Submit for approval.
13. Finalize payroll.
14. Generate individual payslips.

Use this conceptual formula:

Gross Earnings = Sum of applicable earnings components.

Total Deductions = Sum of applicable approved deductions and authorized recoveries.

Net Salary = Gross Earnings − Total Deductions.

The exact salary and payroll formulas must be configurable according to company policy.

Do not invent statutory tax, provident fund, insurance, or other payroll rules that have not been specified.

